// MONDAYS
// Remi Schedule Mondays (sitting at the Beach with Oarfish)
	"SCHEDULE.remi.monday": "Hey, you caught us on a good time. Wanna sit down with us?",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.spring.1": "Whoo, nice to walk out here and smell the fresh scent of spring.$11#$e#Gonna be extra busy again since the snow melted, huh? Everyone smells pretty hectic during the start of every season.#$e#And that means a lot of people smelling like sweat... sigh.$6",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.spring.8": "At least the flowers smell nice around town. I missed those when winter came around.$11#$e#Oarfish smells good all year round, though. Ehehe...$11#$e#...Mmmmm.$u#$b#Ow! Okay, I'll stop.$8",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.spring.15": "This week is filled with alcoholic desires. Get some beer ready if you wanna make some friends.#$e#Dunno what I mean? Check the calendar.$11",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.spring.22": "You're acting weird, Fish. You seeing someone else in this town or something.$6#$e#You're somewhat fond of that glasses guy. Pierre was it?$a#$e#C'mooon, he's a sleaze. He's nothing but selfish desires and he's married. The man smells greasy like the fried calamari he likes so much.$a#$e#Fish, come on now. Look at me.$6#$e#Look at me, Fish. Turn your head my way. Come on, I can't smell your eyes on me yet.$6",

	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.summer.1": "Hoo boy, it's getting really hot. Maybe I should shed my coat...$6#$e#...Nah.#$e#The upside of this hot summer season is that there's ice cream being sold for cheap.$11#$e#Actually, have I told you about the Ice Cream Bypass?#$e#Basically, you get someone else to stand on the otherside of the ice cream stand, and you'd be able to buy ice cream in any season. Neat, huh?#$e#You probably need to get your own companion to do it for you, though... Maybe a loyal steed.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.summer.8": "Hey, you caught us on a good time. Wanna sit down with us?",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.summer.15": "Geez, must be the middle of summer. It's so hot out here.$6#$e#Eh, what do you mean it's just you? It's the pesky sun, silly!$h",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.summer.22": "Ooooh...$10#$e#...Wow.$10#$e#Hehe, these feel really nice, Oarfish. Any more shells to show me?$11#$e#Hey, @. I can smell the end of summer just by the edge of the calendar. Looking forward to spooky season?",

	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.fall.1": "Can you smell that? It's the start of something great.$11#$e#Gonna be a busy season for farmers. What about you? Planning something big?#$e#Fish and I are just gonna enjoy the autumn atmosphere for as long as it lasts.$11",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.fall.8": "I've told you about my best friend back home, right?#$b#She's not with us, but she can keep up to speed with us easily. And I bet she knows a thing or two about you already.#$e#She can see through Oarfish's eyes. It's how our small, independent group do operations.#$e#She's the smart gal that gives us orders and intel all the way from base, and Fish and I do the butt-whooping.#$e#Of course, she telepathically asks Fish for permission before that happens. Don't want her to see \"everything\", hehe.$11",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.fall.15": "Mmmm, I can smell ripe patches of pumpkin in the air. It's gonna be a good harvest.$11#$e#Oh, right. Tomorrow's the fair, right? Good luck and have fun.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.fall.22": "There's a chill in the air, fall is almost over.$6#$e#Fish and I are gonna miss it.",

	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.winter.1": "...A....Ah...$8#$b#AA-CHOO!!$13#$e#Gee, Oarfish. Still hanging out here even when it's freezing?$6#$e#...Yeah, I know. We do this all the time.#$e#Oh hey, @. Feel like sitting in the freezing cold with us? Hehe.$11",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.winter.8": "Brrrr... it's cold. Oarfish can we please hold han-$6#$b#Oh geez!! @, you almost walked in on us.$8#$e#...Huh? Yeah, I agree. It's way too lewd of a public display. What was I thinking...$6",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.winter.15": "%Remi is leaning comfortably on Oarfish's shoulder.#$e#...Hehehe.$u#$e#Hm, shoo. Get your own cuddle-buddy.$6#$e#Whaa?? Oarfish no, what are you doing? Only *I* can lean on you!$13",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.winter.22": "So, Fish. The year is gonna end in a week I think.$6#$b#Should we stay around for another year?#$e#Oh. Geez, @. Can't say anything without you being within earshot.$11#$e#Oarfish and I just agreed we are staying for as long as we still like hanging out around here.#$e#Still, when you grow old and die, Fish and I will probably go back home.$6#$b#Your human lifespan is probably enough time to say we had a short vacation, I think.",

// Oarfish Schedule Mondays (sitting at the Beach with Remi)
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.spring.1": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish briefly greets you. She seems contemplative on how she've spent the last year, and how she'll spend this new year.#$e#...!$h#$b#%Ultimately, she shrugs it away. Anything goes!",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.spring.8": "...#$b#%Oarfish stares at Remi perversely sniffing at her transparent shawl.#$e#...$a#$b#%Oarfish glares at Remi as she got up sniffing on her shoulder.#$b#%She swatted Remi away.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.spring.15": "...#$b#%Oarfish advices you not to prepare beer this week, turning your attention to pizzas and parsnips.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.spring.22": "...#$b#%Oarfish has absolutely no idea what Remi is talking about.#$e#...$7#$b#%Oarfish turns her attention to you, showing interest in what you have to say instead.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.summer.1": "...$h#$b#%Oarfish is enjoying a cone of ice cream.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.summer.8": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish pats on the empty spot next to her.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.summer.15": "...#$b#%Oarfish is fanning herself with a palm leaf.#$e#%A large crab scuttled out from the waters and right towards Oarfish.#$b#...$7#$b#%Oarfish handed the palm leaf to the crab, letting it fan both her and Remi.#$e#...?$7",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.summer.22": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish hands Remi some seashells, each a different shape, size, texture and color.#$e#...$7#$b#%Oarfish greets you. She laid out the seashells on her palms for you to see.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.fall.1": "...!$h#$b#%Oarfish smiles. She seems the happiest once the leaves turn orange.#$e#...$7",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.fall.8": "...$7#$b#...!$u#$b#%Oarfish paused, and then nodded at no one. It seems like she's subtly communicating with someone who isn't here.#$e#...$7#$b#%Oarfish gestures her other friend is presently \"here\", and that she's saying hello to you.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.fall.15": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish rapidly gestures the letters \"GLHF tomorrow\" with one hand. You miraculously got all of that.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.fall.22": "...$l#$b#%Oarfish stares lovingly at the orange leaves, savoring them before everything turns white and blue.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.winter.1": "...$u#$b#%Oarfish sneezed.#$e#...#$b#%Oarfish grabbed at Remi's large sleeves and wiped her pointy nose with it.#$e#...#$b#...?$7",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.winter.8": "...#$b#%Oarfish stares at Remi, judging her indecent attempt to hold her hand.#$e#...$s#$b#...#$b#%Oarfish held Remi's hand. She gestures that she admits she's no better.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.winter.15": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish invites you to sit by her otherside. She gestures that you're free to rest on her shoulder.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.winter.22": "...$s#$b#%Oarfish seems contemplative. She looks up at you with a sad look in her eye.#$e#...$l#$b#%Oarfish reassures you that she and Remi will accompany you for the entire duration of your lifetime. For as long as you want them around.",


// TUESDAYS
// Remi Schedule Tuesdays (eating at the private dinner table at the Saloon with Oarfish)
	"SCHEDULE.remi.tuesday": "Hey, good to see you. Fish and I wanted to have some girls' night out.#$e#We come here on Tuesdays and Saturdays. Less humans that way.#$e#Want me to buy us a meal or something? Don't be shy, you can join us.$11",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.tuesday": "Hey, the whole party's here! Now what do you guys want to order?$9#$e#Me? A simple beer would do.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.spring.2": "Hey, @! Wanna eat with us?$9#$b#Order anything you want. It's still a brand new year.#$e#By the way, Fish is looking forward to this coming Thursday and Sunday. I can figure you know why.#$e#Say, come along with us here every Tuesday. I bet you and Fish can exchange notes about the people in town.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.spring.9": "Still waiting for our orders. Why don't you join us? It's our treat.#$e#Hmm... eggs are on the menu.#$b#Oh, that reminds me. If you're missing out on strawberries this Spring you can get them this Saturday. Don't miss it.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.spring.16": "Beer night!$h#$b#Yup, this week reeks with the stench of beer.#$b#Wanna make friends easy around here? Give 'em a beer.$11#$e#Except, you know. People who don't like beer.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.spring.23": "@! Take a seat with us!$h#$e#Huh? There isn't a third seat?$6#$b#Well, I guess we could request another from Chef Gus.#$e#Flowers' been blooming a lot lately. I can smell an event coming very soon.#$e#Flower Dance?$6#$b#Nah. We ain't going. That's for the young'uns wanting to find love. We're way over that.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.summer.2": "...$a#$b#Oh, @!$10#$b#Don't mind me, I'm just scouting the enemy.$11#$e#Chef Gus is a formidable rival. You could say our weekly dinner dates also doubles as studying the opposition.#$b#I gotta keep up if I still want to call myself a chef.$11",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.summer.9": "I was hoping I wouldn't smell sweaty people from here.$6#$b#Oh hey, @. You mind closing the door for us? It would really help my nose.#$e#I'm craving something cheesy tonight. Like Pepper Poppers and Cheesy Cauli.#$b#What about you, Fish?$11",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.summer.16": "I wonder if there are any more of those fruity selections in Chef Gus' menu?$11#$b#I feel like going for a strawberry shake.#$e#Say, @. You got a blender at home? We could try making experimental shakes with the stuff you grow.#$e#Cave carrot juice? Hmmm...",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.summer.23": "Whoo! Summer nights are making me want a cold one.$9#$b#Come on, let's get ourselves a sundae.$11#$e#Huh? That's not on the menu?$6#$b#Oh well, guess I'll go with beer, then.#$e#Say, @. What's your favorite summer dish?",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.fall.2": "Ahaaa, Fall's really here.$11#$b#You can just taste the crunch in the air.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.fall.9": "Mmmm... This season's making me want hot soup.$11#$e#You growing pumpkins on your farm? Pumpkin soup's gonna be really popular this season. And well, just pumpkins in general.#$e#Stock up on a few pumpkins this year. You never know.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.fall.16": "Heya, any luck at the games?",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.fall.23": "Brrr... I felt that cold evening bite outside earlier.$11#$b#Sit down with us and have a hot soup or drink or something.#$e#So, how's harvest? Selling good this season?",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.winter.2": "@! Glad you can make it!$h#$b#It's really cold out tonight. Stick around and have something warm y'hear?",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.winter.9": "So, did you attend the fishing contest yesterday? How was it?#$e#Heh, Willy sure is formidable, huh? I can respect his affinity with the ocean.$11",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.winter.16": "Hey, @. We'll check out the Night Market in a bit.#$b#Fish has been telling me to see the mermaid.$11#$e#Wait, how will I even see the mermaid?$6#$b#And she sings too, huh?$6#$e#Yeah, I don't think I'm going tonight after all. Sorry, Fish.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.winter.23": "Hey, the whole party's here! Now what do you guys want to order?$9#$e#Year's about to end, so let's make tonight a feast! Cheers!$h",

// Oarfish Schedule Tuesdays (eating at the private dinner table at the Saloon with Remi)
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.tuesday": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish invites you to eat with them.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.tuesday": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish invites you to eat with them.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.spring.2": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish briefly waves at you, before returning to her sketchbook.#$e#...?$7#$b#%You can spot familiar faces in her sketchbook. Particularly, Kent and Lewis.#$e#...!$h#$b#%Upon closer inspection are notes of Oarfish's observations about them.#$b#%Mr. Kent: No bombs. No surprises. Fiddlehead Risotto, Roasted Hazelnuts.#$b#%Mayor Lewis: Try to audit taxes. Autumn's Bounty, Glazed Yams, Green Tea, Vegetable Medley.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.spring.9": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish briefly greets you, before returning to her sketchbook.#$e#...$7#$b#%You can spot familiar faces in her sketchbook. Vincent is on one page, and Haley is on the other.#$e#...!$h#$b#%Upon closer inspection are notes of Oarfish's observations about them.#$b#%Vincent: Check for parasites. Pink Cake, Cranberry Candy, Ginger Ale.#$b#%Haley: Include glitter. Pink Cake, Fruit Salad.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.spring.16": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish briefly gestures hello, before returning to her sketchbook.#$e#...$s#$b#%The sketches seem lifeless than usual. You can spot Pam and Shane.#$e#...#$b#%Upon closer inspection, there are notes detailing their favorite dishes.#$b#%Pam: Parsnip Soup#$b#%Shane: Pepper Poppers, Pizza#$e#...#$b#%There's more.#$b#%Pam: No alcohol.#$b#%Shane: No. Alcohol.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.spring.23": "...$h#$b#%Oarfish smiles at you, and then returns to her sketchbook.#$e#...$7#$b#%You can spot a sketch of Pierre and Emily surrounded by flowers in separate pages.#$e#...!$h#$b#%There are more notes here.#$b#%Pierre: Fried Calamari. Catch a squid later.#$b#%Emily: Is aware of us... friend? Friend. Loves Survival Burger the most.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.summer.2": "...$h#$b#%Oarfish smiles at you. She leans back and lets you take a peek at her sketchbook.#$e#...$7#$b#%On one page is a sketch of Jas playing with cows. On another page is Gus with a flattering mustache.#$e#...!$h#$b#%There are more notes here.#$b#%Jas: Pink Cake, Plum Pudding. Plant fairy roses in Fall.#$b#%Gus: Escargot, Fish Taco, Tropical Curry. Remi, take notes.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.summer.9": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish greets you. She leans back and lets you take a peek at her sketchbook.#$e#...$7#$b#%The theme appears to be clashing interests in science and sports, but drawn to fit together. Maru and Alex are giving each other competitive smirks.#$e#...!$h#$b#%There are more notes here.#$b#%Maru: Cheese Cauliflower, Pepper Poppers, Rhubarb Pie. Boss likes her.#$b#%Alex: Complete Breakfast, Salmon Dinner. Takes a lot of effort.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.summer.16": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish notices you approaching. She leans back and lets you take a peek at her sketchbook.#$e#...$7#$b#%The theme appears to be of contrasting personalities. Sam and Demetrius complement each other with their respective playfulness and seriousness.#$e#...!$h#$b#%Upon closer inspection, there are small notes of Oarfish's thoughts around them.#$b#%Sam: Maple Bar, Pizza. Forgetful. Uses rubber bands as reminders. Maybe Remi would like to try that.#$b#%Demetrius: Bean Hotpot, Ice Cream, Rice Pudding. Reminds me of Boss.#$e#...$7#$b#%Oh, there's another page. A doodle of Dwarf and a few notes.#$b#%Dwarf: Lemon Stone. Murderer.#$b#...!$h",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.summer.23": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish looks up from her sketchbook. She leans back and lets you take a peek.#$e#...$7#$b#%It is a sketch of a man with a fishing rod and a child with ruffled hair standing by the docks and admiring the Moonlight Jellies. The man appears to be Willy.#$e#...!$h#$b#%There are more notes here.#$b#%Willy: Mead. Can take fish raw.#$b#%Child: Poi. Need to learn his name.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.fall.2": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish looks up from her sketchbook and smiled.#$e#...$7#$b#%The theme appears to be about literature. Penny and Elliott are drawn as the reader and writer respectively.#$e#...!$h#$b#%Upon closer inspection, there are more notes surrounding them.#$b#%Penny: Poppyseed Muffin, Red Plate, Roots Platter, Tom Kha Soup. Tiny book lady.#$b#%Elliott: Crab Cakes, Tom Kha Soup. Tall book man.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.fall.9": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish looks up from her sketchbook and smiled. There are a lot of them in a page this time.#$e#...$7#$b#%The first page constrasts Abigail's adventurous youth and Jodi's monotonous life as a mother.#$b#%The second page is a sketch Robin and Marnie and their harmonious professions. Robin builds a barn and Marnie fills it up completely with nothing but pigs...#$e#...!$h#$b#%Along with descriptions are notes detailing their favorite dishes.#$b#%Jodi: Stressed mom. Loves Chocolate Cake and Crispy Bass. Also Pancakes.#$b#%Abigail: Digests rocks. Loves Banana Pudding, Blackberry Cobbler, Chocolate Cake and Spicy Eel. Don't give blackberries by itself.#$b#%Marnie: No meat. Loves Farmer's Lunch, Pink Cake, and Pumpkin Pie.#$b#%Robin: Strong arms. Spaghetti lover. I can respect that.#$e#%There's another page entirely dedicated to Sandy and the desert. You can spot the desert trader and her camel waving from the background.#$b#%Sandy: Not her real name. Mango Sticky Rice. Might need to swim to the next island to get those.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.fall.16": "...$7",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.fall.23": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish looks up from her sketchbook. She leans back and lets you take a peek at a page.#$e#...$7#$b#%It's George with his usual grumpy look. The sketch is very detailed and realistic, showing off his wrinkles and eyebags.#$e#...!$h#$b#%Along with descriptions are notes detailing his favorite dish.#$b#%George: Don't bring up mining. Loves Fried Mushroom.#$e#...$7#$b#%Oh, there's another page. It was a picturesque sketch of the sewers; dark and humid.#$b#%Void Spirit: Friendly. Thanks for taking care of Remi back then! Void Mayonnaise.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.winter.2": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish greets you. She moved her hand away from the page for you to see.#$e#...$7#$b#%It is a sketch contrasting the wild forests and a well-kept personal garden. Linus and Caroline are both enjoying tea in the middle of the metaphorical greenery.#$e#...!$h#$b#%Along with descriptions are notes detailing their favorite dishes.#$b#%Linus: Early man. Loves Blueberry Tart and Dish O' The Sea.#$b#%Caroline: The way to her heart is Green Tea. Also Loves Fish Taco and Tropical Curry.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.winter.9": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish smiles at you. She moved her hand away from the page for you to see.#$e#...$7#$b#%It is a sketch contrasting the personal and impersonal professions of Harvey and Sebastian respectively. There is warmth and coldness in their eyes.#$e#...!$h#$b#%Along with descriptions are notes detailing their favorite dishes.#$b#%Sebastian: Needs more Vitamin D. Loves Pumpkin Soup and Sashimi. Easy prep.#$b#%Harvey: Needs more exercise. Loves Coffee and a Super Meal.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.winter.16": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish waves at you. She moved her hand away from the page for you to see.#$e#...$7#$b#%It is a sketch of two elderly people; one of magic, and one of the mundane. Evelyn's side of the page appears to have more flair to it than the Wizard's.#$e#...!$h#$b#%Along with descriptions are notes detailing their favorite dishes.#$b#%Wizard: Magic man still needs to eat. He can always chew on a Super Cucumber.#$b#%Evelyn: Only the sweetest will suffice. Loves Chocolate Cake and Stuffing.",

	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.winter.23": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish gestures hello. She moved her hand away from the page for you to see..#$e#...$7#$b#%It is a sketch contrasting passion and lifeless profession. On one page, Leah is a sparkling fire of artistic passion. On the other page is Clint striking at the anvil with apathy.#$e#...!$h#$b#%Along with descriptions are notes detailing their favorite dishes.#$b#%Leah: Avoid using additives. Salad, Stir Fry, and Vegetable Medley.#$b#%Clint: Could use a cola. Artichoke Dip and Fiddlehead Risotto",


// WEDNESDAYS
// Remi Schedule Wednesdays (standing by the docks at the Forest)
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.spring.a": "Everything smells so alive around here...$11#$b#Oh hey, you here to relax with us?#$e#Feels nice and breezy out here, huh?",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.spring.b": "Hey, @.#$e#Have you ever thought of growing rows of cherry trees?#$b#Oarfish tells me they look pretty during Spring.#$e#Can't see 'em, but they do have a nice, faint scent once they start blooming. Heh, guess even the blind can enjoy Flower Viewings.$11",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.spring.c": "Nice of you to come here, @.$9#$e#So, what's your favorite season?",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.spring.d": "Good evening, @.#$e#Hm? Yeah. Spring is my birth month. I just like spring.#$e#Hehe, actually, there's a reason why I picked spring to be my birth month. But it's more of an inside joke than anything.$11",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.summer.a": "Here to relax by the pond? Feel free to join us.#$e#I don't like deep waters, but the pond doesn't smell like the ocean, so I'm not as nervous.#$e#...Fish might push me, though.$7#$b#Hey, while you're here, can you keep her from doing that? Thanks.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.summer.b": "Hooboy, it's getting hot.#$b#No, it's not you, @. Hehehe.$11#$e#Seriously, it's hot. Kinda tempting to take a dip in the pond to cool off but...$6#$e#...Oarfish? You're not planning anything, are you?$7",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.summer.c": "Hmm, what's good to eat on a warm summer night like this?$6#$b#Any ideas, @?#$e#Yeah, food is all I could think of most of the time.$11",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.summer.d": "G'eve, @. Hot night, huh?$11#$b#Hmm? Take off my coat?$6#$b#This coat is part of my body, though.$6#$e#Fish is the same. Her shawl and everything is her body, too.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.fall.a": "Everythings smells like crunchy crimson and gold this season. I love it.$11#$e#Yeah, I can sort of smell colors, too.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.fall.b": "Evening. You smell crispy. I like it.#$e#Yup, Fall is Oarfish's birth month.#$b#Could've been winter, but she enjoyed the idea of watching things dying instead of things being already dead.#$e#Yup, that's what she told to me.$11",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.fall.c": "Hey @, what's your favorite color?#$e#Yeah, I know it's a dumb question, but it gives me a taste of what you generally like.$11#$e#Hm? No, I can't taste colors.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.fall.d": "Hey, nice that it ain't so hot anymore, huh?#$e#You wearing something thick? Don't want you getting cold.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.winter.a": "Brrr... It's really cold, but not cold enough to keep us from doing our dock routine.$9#$e#Our bodies normally aren't bothered by extreme temperatures - we can swim in lava if we want to, but Fish and I chose to live out the full Earth experience.#$e#That means lowering the parameters of how much coldness our bodies can tolerate before it stings.$11#$b#...Actually, you know what? I'll stop boring you with the details.",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.winter.b": "I wonder if I can eat the ice... it's just frozen water, right?#$e#Oh, hey @.#$e#What?$6",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.winter.c": "Hey, @. Had dinner already?#$e#So, what hot meal can you recommend in a cold night like this?",
	"SCHEDULE.remi.Marriage.winter.d": "@, good evening.#$e#Good thing the rivers aren't frozen over, huh?#$e#Actually, I wish it was.$6#$b#...$7",

// Oarfish Schedule Wednesdays (standing by the docks at the Forest)
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.spring.a": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish invites you to admire the pond.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.spring.b": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish is happy you're here.#$e#...?$7#$b#%Oarfish wonders if you also enjoy Flower Viewing.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.spring.c": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish gestures you to take it easy.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.spring.d": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish greets you.#$e#...!$h#$b#%Oarfish shows you a sketch of a springy, slinky toy. A note at the bottom says that this is something important to Remi.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.summer.a": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish greets you.#$e#...?#$b#%Oarfish seems puzzled at what Remi is saying.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.summer.b": "...#$b#%Oarfish seems bothered by the evening temperature.#$e#...?$7#$b#%Oarfish gestures she's not planning anything.#$e#...$8",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.summer.c": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish seems to be sipping on a Joja can.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.summer.d": "...#$b#%Oarfish seems to be watching the pond intently.#$e#...!$a#$b#%Suddenly, her shawl moved like two arms quickly snatching a fish out of the water.#$e#...?$7#$b#%Oarfish wonders why you're staring at her like that.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.fall.a": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish seems to enjoy the quiet Autumn night.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.fall.b": "...!$h#$b#%Oarfish seems to be in a good mood this evening.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.fall.c": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish is quietly enjoying the night.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.fall.d": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish is watching the midnight carps swimming in the pond.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.winter.a": "...#$b#%Oarfish seems like she's shivering.",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.winter.b": "...!$h#$b#%Oarfish seems to be forming a perfect ball out of ice with her hands.#$e#...$7#$b#%Oarfish hands Remi the snowball. Remi took a bite.#$b#%Remi: OW!#$b#%There was a rock under the ice.#$e#...?$7",
	"SCHEDULE.oarfish.Marriage.winter.c": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish has a lava eel wrapped around her arms like a snake. It seems to be exuding heat from its body.#$e#...?$7",
